// This correctly fires on every " <<" the model writes anywhere (including
// inline references like "The total is <<n>>").  Constrained mode then traps
// each tiny reference: parser hard-mask generates one valid token (e.g., "n"),
// IsCompletePrefix fires immediately on that single identifier, and CloseSpan
// emits ">>". ~18 tiny single-token spans per example. The evaluator extracts
// the last one — a bare variable — and scores wrong.
//
// Fix strategy (two-phase, no mid-text constrained entry):
//   Phase 1 — Fully unconstrained generation. Let the model write its natural
//   step-by-step solution (including any inline "<<...>>" it generates as free
//   text). Break on EOS.  Reserve 51 steps for Phase 2.
//
//   Phase 2 — ONE forced constrained final-answer span. After Phase 1 ends
//   (EOS or budget-51), call OpenConstrainedSpan (appends "<<"), then
//   CloseSpanWithinBudget with ≥50 steps.  CloseSpanWithinBudget tracks the
//   LONGEST complete parse prefix and closes there, guaranteeing a full
//   combined expression (not a single-token stub).  The evaluator always
//   extracts the LAST "<<...>>" span, which is our forced complete one.
//
//   Guidance instructs the model to reason with symbolic variable names and
//   build toward a single combined formula, priming the constrained generation
//   in Phase 2 to reproduce that formula.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// Invariant 1 — parser_validity:
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//
//   Initial block (insideConstrained = true path):
//     CloseSpanWithinBudget postcondition directly guarantees
//     insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut).
//     If it leaves the span open, the postcondition still guarantees validity.  ✓
//
//   Phase 1 loop:
//     We enter Phase 1 only when insideConstrainedOut = false (the initial block
//     either did not run, or ran and set steps := maxSteps making the loop
//     condition false).  insideConstrainedOut stays false throughout Phase 1
//     because we never call any span-entry helper.  The implication is vacuously
//     true at all loop iterations.  ✓
//
//   Phase 2 — OpenConstrainedSpan:
//     Sets currentConstrainedOut := [] and insideConstrainedOut := true.
//     parser.IsValidPrefix([]) holds by the method precondition.  ✓
//
//   Phase 2 — CloseSpanWithinBudget:
//     Postcondition guarantees insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//     on every exit path (closed or still open).  ✓
//
// Invariant 2 — progress: |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
//
//   Init: equality at steps = 0.  ✓
//
//   Initial block: closeBudget = maxSteps; CloseSpanWithinBudget postcondition
//     gives |generated| <= old + closeBudget = |generatedPrefix| + maxSteps.
//     After steps := maxSteps: |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps.  ✓
//
//   Phase 1 loop: Each iteration increments steps by 1.  EOS path breaks without
//     appending; otherwise generated grows by exactly 1 token.
//     |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps is preserved.  ✓
//
//   Phase 2 — OpenConstrainedSpan: appends exactly 1 token ("<<"); steps += 1.
//     |generated| grows by 1, steps grows by 1.  ✓
//
//   Phase 2 — CloseSpanWithinBudget: closeBudget = maxSteps - steps_before;
//     postcondition |generated| <= old + closeBudget.
//     After steps := maxSteps: |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + maxSteps
//                                           = |generatedPrefix| + steps.  ✓
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END

